= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [The landmark 1972 report published by the Club of Rome warning against industrial resource exhaustion and population collapse was titled:], (
  [Silent Spring], [Our Common Future], [The Limits to Growth], [Agenda 21],
))

#mcq(2, [In which year did the historic Brundtland Commission publish its report 'Our Common Future', popularizing the concept of sustainable development?], (
  [1972], [1987], [1992], [1997],
))

#mcq(3, [The United Nations Conference on Environment and Development (UNCED), popularly known as the Earth Summit, was held in 1992 in which city?], (
  [Stockholm, Sweden], [Kyoto, Japan], [Rio de Janeiro, Brazil], [Johannesburg, South Africa],
))

#mcq(4, [Under the Rio Declaration, which fundamental principle established that developed nations bear a higher moral and legal burden for cleaning up the global environment?], (
  [Absolute Sovereignty Principle], [Common But Differentiated Responsibilities (CBDR)], [Precautionary Principle], [Polluter Never Pays Principle],
))

#mcq(5, [In which year did India formally sign and ratify the Kyoto Protocol on climate change?], (
  [1997], [2000], [August 2002], [December 2015],
))

#mcq(6, [Which of the following is NOT one of the four internationally recognized 'Global Commons'?], (
  [Earth's Atmosphere], [Antarctica], [The Ocean Floor], [The Amazon Rainforest],
))

#mcq(7, [The 1987 Montreal Protocol was a landmark international treaty specifically adopted to address which environmental crisis?], (
  [Global Greenhouse Gas Emissions], [Depletion of the Stratospheric Ozone Layer], [Trade in Endangered Species], [Disposal of Hazardous Chemical Waste],
))

#mcq(8, [The Persian Gulf region in the Middle East accounts for approximately what percentage of the world's total known petroleum oil reserves?], (
  [Barely 15%], [Nearly 30%], [Roughly 64%], [Over 90%],
))

#mcq(9, [How many national missions were formulated under India's National Action Plan on Climate Change (NAPCC) launched in June 2008?], (
  [5 Missions], [8 Missions], [10 Missions], [12 Missions],
))

#mcq(10, [Where is the permanent global headquarters of the treaty-based International Solar Alliance (ISA), co-founded by India and France in 2015, located?], (
  [Paris, France], [New Delhi, India], [Gurugram, India], [Nairobi, Kenya],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [The Club of Rome, an international group of scientists and economists, published 'The Limits to Growth' in 1972, predicting resource depletion from unchecked growth.], answer: [C])

#solution(2, [The Brundtland Commission (World Commission on Environment and Development) released 'Our Common Future' in 1987, defining sustainable development for the world.], answer: [B])

#solution(3, [The UN Earth Summit (UNCED) convened in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, in June 1992, adopting the Rio Declaration, Agenda 21, and the UNFCCC on climate change.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [Principle 7 of the Rio Declaration articulated Common But Differentiated Responsibilities (CBDR), acknowledging developed nations' historical emissions debt.], answer: [B])

#solution(5, [India signed and ratified the Kyoto Protocol in August 2002; as a developing nation, India was exempt from mandatory emission reduction targets under the protocol.], answer: [C])

#solution(6, [The four recognized Global Commons are: the Earth's Atmosphere, Antarctica, the Ocean Floor, and Outer Space. The Amazon Rainforest falls under sovereign state jurisdiction (mainly Brazil).], answer: [D])

#solution(7, [The Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer was adopted in September 1987, successfully mandating the global phase-out of CFCs.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [The Middle East (Persian Gulf) contains approximately 64% of known global oil reserves, making it the strategic cockpit of global energy geopolitics.], answer: [C])

#solution(9, [Prime Minister Manmohan Singh launched the NAPCC in June 2008 with exactly eight national missions covering solar, water, agriculture, energy efficiency, and ecosystems.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [The International Solar Alliance (ISA) is permanently headquartered at the National Institute of Solar Energy (NISE) campus in Gurugram (Haryana), India.], answer: [C])

